156
].
The liver, brain, lungs, and bones are among the typical places where BC metastasises [
157
,
158
]. A prior team used LC-MS/MS-based targeted metabolomics and lipidomics to analyse plasma and track the progression of pulmonary metastasis in mice after inoculation with 4T1 metastatic BC cells. They discovered that changes in the arginase (ARG) pathway may indicate early-stage cancer metastasis and may be a target for future therapy [
159
]. According to K. Kus et al., modifications in glycolysis, lipid signalling, and structure may serve as potential biomarkers for aggressive cancer and late-stage metastasis. When examining the urine metabolites of BALB/c mice using NMR spectroscopy, a study team discovered that taurine, trimethylamine, creatine + phosphocreatine, and trimethylamine-N-oxide were all more plentiful in the early phase and that creatinine and allantoin had dramatically reduced [
